Not sourced from the repository, observed while writing this: a "#"
inside the awk regex ends the make line as a comment even inside
$(shell ...), and "\#" reaches awk, which warns about an unknown
regexp escape. The shebang is therefore matched as the string
"\043!", awk's octal escape for "#!".

With this commit alone, make lint is red on two plugins: claude-rebase
for its reserved name, and git-rebase-i for its frontmatter, which the
cc/git-rebase-i-review topic fixes. After both topics are merged only
claude-rebase remains.
